Hi Judith,

I've attached the exercise with my comments, v0.2. Of the twenty references, =
sixteen looked right to me; I've left the four doubtful candidates in place a=
nd added the leaves and lines I think we should check together before changin=
g the working chapter.

The summaries for 185r and 186r are close enough that I can see how I might c=
hoose the first one too quickly. This afternoon could we open both and look t=
ogether at the sentences on collecting the arrears before a book is taken awa=
y and handing them to the treasurer? I'd also like to keep the preceding perm=
ission to read in the room in view.

Thanks,
Florian

On 14 November 2025 at 15:42, Judith Morris wrote:

> Please open each reference independently first and locate the passage in it=
s surrounding lines. A search result in the transcription file can help you f=
ind a place, but it cannot stand in for opening the source. If a candidate lo=
oks doubtful, leave it as written and note why rather than changing it ahead =
of our comparison.

